.TH WADB 1 "2026-09-22" "wadb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wadb \- pair Android devices over ADB Wi\-Fi via a terminal QR code or
pairing code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B pair
.I host:port
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B connect
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B devices
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B disconnect
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B doctor
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B capabilities
.br
.B wadb
.RI [ flags ]
.B schema
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wadb
prints a QR code in the terminal. Scanning it from
.B Settings \(-> Developer options \(-> Wireless debugging \(-> Pair device with QR code
on an Android 11+ device pairs the device with this host and connects it over
ADB Wi\-Fi, then
.B wadb
exits.
.PP
This is the same protocol Android Studio uses for
.IR "Pair device using Wi-Fi" .
The phone and the host must share a Wi\-Fi network with no AP isolation, and
Wireless debugging must be enabled in Developer options.
.PP
Options may appear before or after a command.
.PP
.B wadb
generates a single\-use service name and password, renders them as a QR code,
waits for the device to announce
.B _adb\-tls\-pairing._tcp
over mDNS, and runs
.BR "adb pair" .
It then waits for the
.B _adb\-tls\-connect._tcp
announce and runs
.BR "adb connect" .
The TLS pairing handshake itself is handled by
.BR adb (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI pair " host:port"
Pair using the address and six\-digit code shown by
.B Wireless debugging \(-> Pair device with pairing code
on the Android device. The code is requested without echoing it to the
terminal. After pairing,
.B wadb
discovers the device's separate connection endpoint and connects automatically.
IPv6 addresses must be enclosed in brackets.
.TP
.B connect
Reconnect a device that is already paired with this host, without printing a QR
code. Pairing survives reboots and Wi\-Fi changes, but the port Android listens
on does not, so this is the command to reach for when a known device stops
appearing in
.BR "adb devices" .
.TP
.B devices
List devices known to
.B adb
alongside Wireless debugging endpoints from a direct mDNS scan and the adb
mDNS cache. Connected devices include their adb state and model; endpoints
that are announcing but not connected are shown as
.BR discovered .
Use
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect a wireless device selected with
.BR \-\-device ,
or every TCP/IP device with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.B doctor
Report the local
.BR adb ,
its platform\-tools version, the network interfaces worth passing to
.BR \-\-iface ,
and the mDNS services
.B adb
can see.
.TP
.B capabilities
Describe the agent-facing command contract without starting
.B adb
or scanning the network. With
.BR "\-\-output json" ,
the response lists commands, side effects, user-action and standard-input
requirements, stable error codes, and the published JSON Schema path.
.TP
.B schema
Print the version 1 structured-output JSON Schema embedded in the binary.
With
.BR "\-\-output json" ,
the schema is returned inside the standard response envelope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-adb " path"
Path to the adb binary. By default
.B wadb
looks in $ANDROID_HOME, $ANDROID_SDK_ROOT, the standard Android Studio SDK
locations, $PATH, and the Homebrew commandline\-tools directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-iface " name"
Browse for mDNS on a single network interface instead of all of them. Use this
when a VPN tunnel, a container bridge, or a second NIC swallows the multicast
traffic. An unusable name is rejected immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-pair\-only
Pair the device, then exit without running
.BR "adb connect" .
Useful when pairing succeeds but the device delays or hides its connect
announce.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-ascii
Render the QR code with plain ASCII blocks, for fonts and emulators that render
half blocks poorly.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-invert
Invert the QR code, for terminals with a light background.
.TP
.B \-\-qr\-sixel
Render the QR code as a sixel image. Requires a terminal that implements the
sixel protocol, and scans under any color theme.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print discovered mDNS service entries to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Never prompt for input on a terminal. Pairing by code remains available when
the six-digit code is supplied through redirected standard input. QR pairing
returns
.B interactive_required
instead of displaying a code or waiting for a scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-pair\-timeout " duration"
How long to wait for the pairing announce. Default 2m.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect\-timeout " duration"
How long to wait for the connect announce. Default 30s.
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-timeout " duration"
How long the
.B devices
and
.B disconnect
commands scan for Wireless debugging announces. Default 3s.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " selector"
Select a device by stable serial, address, host, or full mDNS instance. Used by
.B connect
and
.BR disconnect ;
also filters
.BR devices .
.TP
.B \-\-all
Operate on every matching wireless device. Supported by
.B connect
and
.BR disconnect .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write the backward-compatible v1.2 machine-readable array output. Supported by
.BR devices ,
.BR connect ,
.BR disconnect .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " format"
Select
.B text
or the versioned
.B json
response envelope. Structured JSON is supported by pairing with a code,
capability discovery, diagnostics, device listing, connect, disconnect, and
version output. Progress
and diagnostics remain on standard error. Interactive QR pairing does not
support structured output; use pairing by code instead.
When multiple devices are available,
.B connect \-\-output json
requires an explicit
.B \-\-device
or
.BR \-\-all .
Structured errors include
.B retryable
and
.B requires_user_action
booleans. The complete version 1 contract is published as
.B schemas/wadb-output-v1.schema.json
and can be retrieved from an installed binary with
.BR "wadb schema" .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.B \-v
is a shorthand.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every option above has an environment equivalent; command\-line flags override
it.
.TP
.B WADB_ADB
Same as
.BR \-\-adb .
.TP
.B WADB_IFACE
Same as
.BR \-\-iface .
.TP
.B WADB_PAIR_ONLY
Same as
.BR \-\-pair\-only .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_ASCII
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-ascii .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_INVERT
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-invert .
.TP
.B WADB_QR_SIXEL
Same as
.BR \-\-qr\-sixel .
.TP
.B WADB_VERBOSE
Same as
.BR \-\-verbose .
.TP
.B WADB_NON_INTERACTIVE
Same as
.BR \-\-non\-interactive .
.TP
.B WADB_PAIR_TIMEOUT
Same as
.BR \-\-pair\-timeout .
.TP
.B WADB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
Same as
.BR \-\-connect\-timeout .
.TP
.B WADB_SCAN_TIMEOUT
Same as
.BR \-\-scan\-timeout .
.TP
.B WADB_DEVICE
Same as
.BR \-\-device .
.TP
.B WADB_ALL
Same as
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.B WADB_JSON
Same as
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B WADB_OUTPUT
Same as
.BR \-\-output .
.PP
Boolean variables accept values such as true, false, 1, or 0. Duration
variables accept values such as 30s or 3m.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Paired and connected, or the requested command completed.
.TP
.B 1
Pairing, discovery, or connecting failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or environment values.
.PP
With
.BR "\-\-output json" ,
nonzero exits still write one structured error to standard output. Stable error
codes include
.BR invalid_arguments ,
.BR interactive_required ,
.BR adb_not_found ,
.BR device_not_found ,
.BR multiple_devices ,
.BR discovery_timeout ,
.BR pairing_failed ,
.BR connection_failed ,
and
.BR disconnect_failed .
.SH EXAMPLES
Pair and connect a new device:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb
.EE
.RE
.PP
Pair using the address and code displayed by Android:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb pair 192.168.1.20:37123
.EE
.RE
.PP
Reconnect a device paired earlier, over a specific interface:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb \-\-iface en0 connect
.EE
.RE
.PP
List connected and discovered devices:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb devices
.EE
.RE
.PP
Connect a specific device, then disconnect all wireless devices:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb connect \-\-device RF8M1234ABC
wadb disconnect \-\-all
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose a discovery problem:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb doctor
wadb \-\-verbose
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inspect the agent-facing contract:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wadb capabilities \-\-non\-interactive \-\-output json
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1)
.PP
Project home: https://github.com/LinDevHard/wadb
